WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.320
SCP-682, the indestructible reptile, versus
SCP-1237, the epsilon wave, who would win?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:06.560
In an attempt to terminate SCP-682, the Foundation
gave us the answer.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.000
SCP-1237 is a brain pattern occurring in deep
REM sleep that allows an individual's dreams

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.160
to shape and affect reality when they wake.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:20.560
One specimen affected by SCP-1237 was permitted
to observe SCP-682 and was instructed to dream

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.080
that SCP-682 was a small house cat with no
anomalous abilities, and that the Foundation

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.920
had successfully terminated it.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.920
Seven seconds into their sleep, the subject
seized violently and died less than a minute

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.040
later, alongside 13 other observing security
personnel.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.120
Their bodies were covered with scratches and
bites, as well as symptoms of toxoplasmosis

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.400
and bubonic plague.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.440
Inside SCP-682’s chamber was a small house
cat, licking blood from its coat of fur.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.280
It regenerated into SCP-682 only a few hours
later.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.840
Looks like in this matchup, the lizard, not
the cat, got the foundation’s tongue, as

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:54.560
expected.

